From 68086dd9003c6f6bd146e5d3c44f5b2d0eb0aad5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chaorenex1 <24537608z@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 03:55:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Let a plugin keep a turn open after a text answer

The stop gates could only continue a turn for code edits (pre_verify) or the
kanban protocol, so a plugin that found a blocker while the final model call ran
had no way to act on it. Drain hermes_cli.plugin_runtime's continuation slot
before verify-on-stop, append the text as a durable user row typed
display_kind=adviser, and bound the behaviour with agent.max_plugin_continuations
(default 2, separate from the verify budget). An over-budget request is discarded
with token state expired, so the plugin returns its rows to pending instead of
assuming delivery.
